# Frontend Patterns

## Stack

React + TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, @tanstack/react-query, react-router-dom, lucide-react.

## Navigation Architecture

The frontend uses a **modular sidebar** with collapsible sections:

- `navigation/modules.ts` — Module registry defining sidebar sections (Options, Research, etc.)
- Each module declares its routes, icon, and sub-items
- **Hybrid collapsibility:** Opening one section auto-collapses others; user can manually toggle
- "BETA" badge displayed next to the Tyche logo
- "TRADIER" (sandbox/live) badge displayed under the Options section header
- Settings lives under the Options module (it's options-specific)

## API Layer

- `api/client.ts` — typed `request<T>()` wrapper around fetch. All endpoints under `/api/v1`. Parses FastAPI 422 validation errors into human-readable strings. Includes per-request timing via `performance.now()` and reports errors/slow requests to the telemetry library.
- `hooks/useApi.ts` — react-query hooks wrapping every API call. Mutations invalidate relevant query keys.
- `types/index.ts` — must match backend response shapes exactly. Update when backend changes. Includes `ScanHistoryEntry`.
- `lib/telemetry.ts` — Batched frontend telemetry reporter. Queues error, timing, and crash events in an in-memory buffer (max 50). Flushes to `POST /api/v1/telemetry/events` every 10s or on page unload. Auto-starts on import.

## Error Handling

- `components/ErrorBoundary.tsx` — Class component wrapping `<App />` in `main.tsx`. Catches React render crashes via `componentDidCatch`, reports to `telemetry.reportCrash()`, and shows a recovery UI with a "Reload Page" button.
- API errors are reported via `telemetry.reportError()` in `client.ts`. Network failures (status 0) are tagged with `network_error: true`.
- Slow requests (>5s) are automatically reported as timing events.

## Pages

| Page | Purpose | Key hooks |
|---|---|---|
| Dashboard | Overview, quick links | `useOrderIntents("pending")` |
| Scanner | Full scan (broker + LLM) → persisted results | `useTriggerScan`, `useLatestScan`, `useScanHistory`, `useScanById` |
| Conviction | EMA trend analysis with ladder view | `useConvictionScan`, `useTriggerConvictionScan` |
| Intents | Approve/reject trade recommendations | `useOrderIntents`, `useApproveIntent`, `useRejectIntent` |
| Orders | Open orders + executed trades | `useOpenOrders`, `useOrderIntents("executed")` |
| Monitor | Track positions, real-time P&L + alerts | `useTrackedPositions`, `useTrackPosition` |
| Settings | Editable config (watchlist, capital, risk, universe filters) | `useSystemConfig`, `useUpdateConfig` |

## UI Conventions

- **Light theme** — modern financial broker aesthetic (no dark mode)
- Conviction colors: high=emerald, medium=amber, low=red, none=gray
- Alert severity: critical=red, warning=amber, info=gray
- Risk-failed items: red border + "RISK FAILED" badge
- Risk summary reasons: `FAIL:` prefix=red, `WARN:`=amber, plain=gray
- Empty states must show explanatory messages, not blank space
- `StatusBadge` for labels, `PLValue` for P&L numbers, `Card` for sections (accepts `ReactNode` title)
- Scanner shows `PipelineFunnel` visualization and `RecentScans` history selector
- Conviction page shows expandable `GateLadder` rows for each ticker's eligibility progression

## Scanner Page Components

- `EntryTimingBanner` — Day-of-week-aware banner: green for Tue/Wed (optimal), amber for Thu/Fri (weaker), gray for weekend/Mon. Shows trading window and prime slot guidance.
- `PipelineFunnel` — Shows each filter stage (fundamental, market cap, conviction, institutional) with counts
- `TickerGroupRow` — Groups CSP candidates by ticker with expand/collapse
- `RecentScans` — Collapsible scan history selector, loads full scan details on selection
- `AllocationSummaryCard` — Optimizer-selected trades with gross premium, commission ($0.65/contract), net premium, capital deployed. Includes collapsible trade detail table.
- `AllocationPlayground` — Interactive "what-if" tool inside AllocationSummaryCard:
  - Toggle trades on/off via checkboxes, adjust contract counts with +/- buttons
  - Capital ceiling from `useSystemConfig().available_capital`; blocks increases that exceed limit
  - "Add from N other candidates" dropdown to pull in unselected CSP candidates
  - Side-by-side comparison grid: Recommended vs Your Selection (contracts, premium, commission, net, capital)
  - "Reset to Recommended" button restores optimizer defaults
  - All math is client-side only — no backend call
- `LlmAnalysesCard` — AI analyses sorted by assignment comfort desc, then confidence desc (safest trades first)
- Scan results persist in SQLite — `GET /scanner/latest` returns 200 + null if no scan exists (not 404)
- `useScanHistory(limit)` and `useScanById(scanId)` hooks for history navigation

## Scanner Types

- `AllocatedTrade` — per-trade data from MILP allocator (symbol, strike, expiration, contracts, total_premium, collateral, conviction, etc.)
- `AllocationSummary` — optimizer rollup (total_premium, capital_utilization_pct, solver_status). Persisted version has fewer fields than live — use optional types.
- `ScanResult.allocated_trades` — array of `AllocatedTrade[]` returned by both live and persisted scan endpoints

## Monitor Page

Tracked positions are **in-memory only** on the backend — lost on restart. The position card shows live data from Tradier (underlying price, option bid/ask, greeks, P&L). When Tradier data is unavailable (market closed), a fallback status is returned with an info alert.

Option symbol matching: first tries exact match, then falls back to strike + option type match (handles format mismatches between user input and Tradier OCC format).
